# ezHealthKonnect — Trivy CVE suppression list
#
# POLICY:
#   Only suppress CVEs where --ignore-unfixed still flags them (i.e. the fix
#   exists upstream but hasn't landed in Alpine yet, OR no fix exists at all).
#   Never suppress a CVE that has a released fix we could apply.
#
# REVIEW: Check this file monthly. Remove any CVE once a fix is available
#   by running:  trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed <image>
#   If the CVE no longer appears, its fix has shipped — remove it from here.
#
# FORMAT:  CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # package@version | reason | added YYYY-MM-DD
#
# ── Currently suppressed (no upstream fix in Alpine as of 2026-03-31) ────────
#
# ADD CVEs HERE after reviewing the first scan output.
# Example:
# CVE-2023-44487  # nghttp2 | HTTP/2 rapid reset - Alpine fix pending | added 2026-03-31
